{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/334647-is-hardness-useful","id":334647,"title":"Is Hardness Useful?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-08T17:04:46-08:00","id":334647,"title":"Is Hardness Useful?","content":"I am trying to figure out by-the-book Hardness.<br /> <br /> Since Soak subtracts from levels of damage (usually), and it is difficult to gain Hardness in excess of your Soak, I do not understand the purpose of this mechanic.<br /> <br /> Is there something I am missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3712-quantumpants","name":"QuantumPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T19:08:35-08:00","id":334729,"title":"","content":"Hardness, in Scion 1e RAW, is pretty weak. It's something that's a holdover from Exalted 2e that didn't really need to get ported over.<br /> <br /> However, remember that Hardness kicks in compared to the raw damage dice pool, not the rolled damage. It basically protects you from lucky hits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T22:07:56-08:00","id":334830,"title":"","content":"It's basically just an editing error. There are no useful sources of hardness in the game. It was useful in Exalted, since Exalted as minimum damage pools to circumvent massive soak. Scion lacks that minimum &quot;ping&quot; damage mechanic, making Hardness virtually useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:31:54-08:00","id":341236,"title":"","content":"Yes! Very useful for my character who was eaten by a snake (and had her hardness preventing a lot of the 'being digested' damage- ie. environ effects and squeezing); and semi useful for when falling from a penthouse window to the ground at hero level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2556-firstaide","name":"Firstaide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:58:41-08:00","id":341250,"title":"","content":"Why would her soak not do that instead of hardness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T21:17:44-08:00","id":341528,"title":"","content":"Technically, Hardness would stop environmental damage first, though it is unlikely to have mattered with Soak as it is.<br /> <br /> Part of the issue is that Hardness from armor isn't really a thing (like it is in Exalted 2e); so things like falling which is Piercing, doesn't come into play as making Hardness more valuable.<br /> <br /> If you somehow had 25B Hardness, and 25B Soak, 10 of which was from armor, Hardness would make a difference. But well, that's not exactly going to happen frequently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T21:49:38-08:00","id":345429,"title":"","content":"Hardness isn't always useful for your Scion but it can be dead handy for your mortal allies against other similarly lowe(er) powered problems. Obviously it won't protect them against hydrae or stymphalian bird feathers but when you have Mob mooks that you're using to take over the local crime scene, or just bodyguards who keep the mortal populace in check so you can eat or rest up, having them immune to firearm fire and the like has some significant use. Good for peace of mind too. When your Scion has a teenaged daughter in school it's a little peace of mind to know that she could take a shotgun blast and still walk away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T22:26:32-08:00","id":345447,"title":"","content":"Again, what does Hardness offer that Soak doesn't? Since Scion lacks minimum damage, they're effective the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T01:32:54-08:00","id":345553,"title":"","content":"1) Hardness isn't effected by piercing (much more relevant for Squee's point on mortals and soak).<br /> 2) Hardness compares to the raw dice pool value, where Soak compares to successes. This technically means that Hardness sets in before either 10s counting as double or bonus successes to damage apply in the order of operations.<br /> <br /> Neither of these guarantee Hardness will matter (and with how Scion is written it pretty much guarantees it doesn't), but it means that Hardness has a valid space in 1e's rules. It was just never used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T02:56:04-08:00","id":345602,"title":"","content":"Valid points, but since there is only one single way of gaining Hardness (the 2nd rank Guardian Boon, Aegis) in the entire system, it seems extremely unlikely that it will ever be an issue. An Aegis can only be used on mortals. So a Scion is <i>never</i> going to have a Hardness rating. Inanimate objects have Hardness, wards created by the Ward Boon have Hardness, and Aegis can grant Hardness to mortals or objects, but there is no &quot;natural&quot; Hardness. Scions will <i>always</i> have a Hardness of 0, as will Gods, Demigods and mystical critters.<br /> <br /> The ability of Hardness to by-pass Epic Strength is a pretty big argument that the mechanic does <i>not</i> fit into Scion. Again, the existence of the mechanic is basically an editing mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T03:21:27-08:00","id":345615,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why you're arguing on these points Telgar. I'm not championing Hardness RAW as being implemented well. You asked what Hardness can do that Soak can't. I answered. In my answer I flat out said that the way Scion is RAW, Hardness is useless except maybe in a few very edge cases (which is basically Aegis in application). All of my posts to this thread have not been pro-Hardness as written.<br /> <br /> And Hardness' ability to stop Epic Strength, while impressive, is fundamentally nullified by Epic Dexterity which can easily generate enough extra raw damage dice to overcome Hardness and let all that Epic Strength come blasting through.<br /> <br /> And since we're feeling a bit pendantic about this, it isn't an editing error. It's a design error. There's no mistake in how Hardness is written. There's a giant gaping hole in how the system design uses it (and the very questionable choice of even bothering to include it in the design if you're almost never going to use it in a meaningful way); though it is possible that it was originally supposed to be fairly useless/inaccessible at Hero and was supposed to matter more in the later books, but they never got around to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}